WEBVTT

00:00:11.180 --> 00:00:15.500
<i>The publication of the method to create 
the Wam, an infinite energy device,</i>

00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:18.150
<i>has had a massive effect on society.</i>

00:00:19.050 --> 00:00:25.760
<i>Meanwhile, Shindo Kojiro devises a plan to 
move Kado from its spot at Haneda Airport.</i>

00:00:25.760 --> 00:00:29.190
<i>With the help of Asano Shuhei of the 
Metropolitan Police, he puts it into effect.</i>

00:00:30.190 --> 00:00:34.040
<i>The plan costs an incredible 
amount of manpower and labor,</i>

00:00:34.040 --> 00:00:36.510
<i>but Kado is successfully 
moved to Sayama Lake</i>

00:00:36.510 --> 00:00:38.510
<i>in the south end of Saitama Prefecture.</i>

00:00:39.460 --> 00:00:45.020
<i>But there, Yaha-kui zaShunina shows 
Shindo a new anisotropic device,</i>

00:00:45.020 --> 00:00:47.370
<i>following his sharing of the Wam.</i>

00:02:22.850 --> 00:02:25.160
Sansa

00:02:35.250 --> 00:02:36.840
Hi, SETTEN.

00:02:37.530 --> 00:02:38.910
Anisotropic being.

00:02:43.210 --> 00:02:45.810
Yaha-kui zaShunina.

00:02:44.320 --> 00:02:46.970
<b>Adam Ward</b>

00:02:46.970 --> 00:02:56.040
Asking about the Wam and the anisotropic

00:02:46.970 --> 00:02:56.040
<b>How should we react to the anisotropic?</b>

00:02:47.960 --> 00:02:50.440
<i>So you see, there are still</i>

00:02:50.440 --> 00:02:53.110
<i>many mysteries about the anisotropic.</i>

00:02:53.110 --> 00:02:55.340
<i>Thank you, Gonno-san.</i>

00:02:56.520 --> 00:02:59.440
<i>There's still much confusion 
surrounding the anisotropic issue,</i>

00:02:57.750 --> 00:03:03.120
<b>The Benefits of Using the Wam 
Is Dependency on the Wam Dangerous?</b>

00:02:59.440 --> 00:03:03.120
<i>but many people are talking about 
the benefits the Wam have to offer.</i>

00:03:03.430 --> 00:03:08.100
<i>However, if we were to restructure our 
society to be dependent on the Wam,</i>

00:03:06.700 --> 00:03:09.620
You seem upset, Gonno-san.

00:03:08.100 --> 00:03:11.430
<i>then suddenly became unable 
to use them any longer,</i>

00:03:10.170 --> 00:03:13.860
This is the first time I've felt this way
since I got into the news business.

00:03:11.430 --> 00:03:15.100
<i>would we be able to deal 
with what might follow?</i>

00:03:13.860 --> 00:03:15.900
The method to create the Wam is spreading,

00:03:15.100 --> 00:03:18.760
<i>In other words, instead of 
relying fully on the Wam...</i>

00:03:15.900 --> 00:03:18.760
and the world is in the midst of a revolution.

00:03:19.260 --> 00:03:21.810
All I'd have to do is step outside with a camera,

00:03:21.810 --> 00:03:23.860
and every photo I'd take 
will end up in textbooks.

00:03:24.540 --> 00:03:27.930
But my head's telling me something weird.

00:03:29.210 --> 00:03:31.890
This place has already 
been passed by, it says.

00:03:31.890 --> 00:03:33.570
It's not the front line?

00:03:34.010 --> 00:03:34.900
Yeah.

00:03:35.570 --> 00:03:37.110
That's true.

00:03:37.110 --> 00:03:40.530
The only "front line" right now 
is under the shadow of Kado.

00:03:40.910 --> 00:03:43.130
Want to go switch with 
whoever's staking it out now?

00:03:45.580 --> 00:03:46.450
There you are!

00:03:46.450 --> 00:03:47.990
Gonno, come with me, now!

00:03:47.990 --> 00:03:49.750
You've got one hell of a visitor!

00:03:54.380 --> 00:03:56.290
SETTEN? That SETTEN?

00:03:56.290 --> 00:03:57.450
Yeah.

00:03:57.450 --> 00:03:59.280
Three trillion yen in sales.

00:03:59.280 --> 00:04:00.760
Market capitalization of 100 trillion.

00:04:01.170 --> 00:04:04.050
The largest internet service 
company in the world,

00:04:04.050 --> 00:04:08.060
and the man who built it, one of the 
most important people of our era...

00:04:09.510 --> 00:04:13.010
SETTEN's CEO, Adam Ward.

00:04:14.930 --> 00:04:17.190
You want to talk to me personally?

00:04:17.190 --> 00:04:19.950
You're the one who took this video, right?

00:04:19.950 --> 00:04:21.110
Yes, why?

00:04:21.110 --> 00:04:23.630
It's had two billion views.

00:04:23.630 --> 00:04:25.630
This video, which was taken just one hour

00:04:25.630 --> 00:04:28.330
after the anisotropic object 
known as Kado appeared,

00:04:28.330 --> 00:04:32.330
is the real truth, from before 
the government got involved.

00:04:32.330 --> 00:04:36.080
And that met the needs of 
users all over the world.

00:04:37.290 --> 00:04:40.250
In other words, you're here 
to pay me the ad revenue

00:04:40.250 --> 00:04:42.700
from that illegally uploaded video?

00:04:42.700 --> 00:04:44.590
I've got about that much 
ready for this proposal.

00:04:45.550 --> 00:04:47.730
This is headhunting, Gonno.

00:04:47.730 --> 00:04:50.470
I want you to work for SETTEN.

00:04:51.790 --> 00:04:54.000
And I want you to go report.

00:04:54.000 --> 00:04:54.850
On what?

00:04:55.640 --> 00:04:58.020
What humanity wants to
know about the most.

00:04:59.230 --> 00:05:00.900
Yaha-kui zaShunina.

00:05:08.610 --> 00:05:09.670
Gonno-san!

00:05:17.220 --> 00:05:19.400
NNK is a good station.

00:05:19.400 --> 00:05:23.840
It's a company that takes pride in its 
journalism, with its feet on the ground.

00:05:23.840 --> 00:05:25.350
We know.

00:05:25.350 --> 00:05:28.050
Still, we want to follow you!

00:05:28.460 --> 00:05:32.170
I can't guarantee your safety,
and this is likely to be illegal, too.

00:05:32.770 --> 00:05:35.520
Screw up, and you could get arrested.

00:05:35.520 --> 00:05:38.020
We're prepared for that.

00:05:38.020 --> 00:05:42.050
And how is that different from what 
we've done so far, Gonno-san?

00:05:43.420 --> 00:05:44.440
That's true.

00:05:45.090 --> 00:05:47.070
You're right.

00:05:48.160 --> 00:05:50.160
<b>I can't dry my laundry!</b>

00:05:48.160 --> 00:05:50.160
<b>Give back the sun!!</b>

00:05:48.160 --> 00:05:50.160
<b>Remove Kado now!!</b>

00:05:48.160 --> 00:05:50.160
Give back our peaceful lives!

00:05:50.160 --> 00:05:52.330
Get out!

00:05:52.330 --> 00:05:54.870
Give back the sun!

00:06:10.390 --> 00:06:12.890
Temporary Residence 1 
For Use by the Anisotropic Being in This Universe

00:06:21.130 --> 00:06:22.590
Working hard, you two?

00:06:22.590 --> 00:06:23.770
Natsume-san!

00:06:23.770 --> 00:06:25.570
It's good to see you.

00:06:25.570 --> 00:06:26.570
Hanamori-san!

00:06:27.700 --> 00:06:29.210
Hanamori-san!

00:06:30.450 --> 00:06:31.370
Yes!

00:06:31.370 --> 00:06:34.930
I am Hanamori, special ambassador 
from Japan to the anisotropic!

00:06:34.930 --> 00:06:36.330
Uh... Huh?

00:06:36.330 --> 00:06:38.500
I brought you a present, Hanamori-kun.

00:06:40.120 --> 00:06:42.270
Natsume-san!

00:06:43.350 --> 00:06:46.300
Kado castella cake and Kado buns 
that they're selling nearby.

00:06:46.300 --> 00:06:50.430
Kado comes here, and instead of running, 
they find a way to market it.

00:06:50.430 --> 00:06:54.090
Humans are pretty strong creatures.

00:06:54.090 --> 00:06:56.060
It looks like things are rough here.

00:06:56.630 --> 00:06:58.830
There's so much to work out 
with the government bureaus.

00:06:58.830 --> 00:07:01.020
I can't do it all by myself.

00:07:01.020 --> 00:07:02.640
Where's Shindo-kun?

00:07:02.640 --> 00:07:04.570
He's meeting with zaShunina.

00:07:04.910 --> 00:07:07.960
He's spent nearly all of the past 
couple of days inside Kado.

00:07:07.960 --> 00:07:11.030
Well, that is his job, but...

00:07:15.690 --> 00:07:18.450
The choppers are so loud, 
I can't even take a nap.

00:07:18.940 --> 00:07:23.210
Since this isn't a rescue site, they feel 
like they can get as close as they want.

00:07:23.530 --> 00:07:26.120
Should we give them a warning?

00:07:28.920 --> 00:07:30.130
Aren't they too close?

00:07:30.550 --> 00:07:31.970
Yeah.

00:07:31.970 --> 00:07:33.080
Take a look.

00:07:33.080 --> 00:07:34.200
What helicopter is that?

00:07:34.200 --> 00:07:35.000
Yes, sir.

00:07:37.400 --> 00:07:39.060
Agata-san, that's SETTEN.

00:07:40.770 --> 00:07:45.520
<i>This is Gonno Takuma with 
the SETTEN broadcast team.</i>

00:07:45.520 --> 00:07:48.150
Anisotropic being, Yaha-kui zaShunina,

00:07:48.570 --> 00:07:50.400
<i>we want to interview you!</i>

00:07:51.900 --> 00:07:52.900
Get a chopper up there!

00:07:52.900 --> 00:07:54.510
The fuel's not warmed up!

00:07:54.510 --> 00:07:55.460
Damn it!

00:07:54.510 --> 00:07:55.950
It's gonna take five minutes!

00:07:57.170 --> 00:07:59.070
Attention, civilian helicopter.

00:07:59.070 --> 00:08:01.080
<i>This is the JGSDF.</i>

00:08:01.080 --> 00:08:03.330
<i>You have not been given 
permission to approach Kado.</i>

00:08:03.810 --> 00:08:07.140
<i>Please leave this area immediately.</i>

00:08:07.140 --> 00:08:10.430
<i>If you ignore this warning, 
we will respond with force.</i>

00:08:10.430 --> 00:08:11.980
"Force"?

00:08:11.980 --> 00:08:14.500
It means we can stay 
until they force us out.

00:08:15.090 --> 00:08:16.390
Yaha-kui zaShunina,

00:08:17.080 --> 00:08:20.050
<i>what the world wants now is information!</i>

00:08:20.690 --> 00:08:22.090
<i>About the anisotropic,</i>

00:08:22.090 --> 00:08:23.190
<i>about Kado,</i>

00:08:23.550 --> 00:08:25.560
<i>and about you!</i>

00:08:25.560 --> 00:08:27.450
<i>All humanity wants to know!</i>

00:08:28.020 --> 00:08:29.560
But more than anything...

00:08:30.070 --> 00:08:31.530
We want to know!

00:08:31.930 --> 00:08:36.010
<i>Please, grant us an interview, 
Yaha-kui zaShunina!</i>

00:08:39.650 --> 00:08:41.720
Gonno-san, I don't think...

00:08:41.720 --> 00:08:42.540
Look!

00:08:52.050 --> 00:08:53.260
He accepted!

00:08:53.680 --> 00:08:55.010
Yes!

00:09:02.770 --> 00:09:04.300
Should we arrest them?

00:09:04.300 --> 00:09:05.270
We can't.

00:09:05.660 --> 00:09:10.030
The anisotropic was given a 
degree of extralegal authority

00:09:10.030 --> 00:09:13.880
within Japan after the negotiations.

00:09:14.570 --> 00:09:17.970
We can make requests, but we 
can't force him to do anything.

00:09:28.170 --> 00:09:32.470
Shindo Kojiro, the representative 
of the anisotropic.

00:09:42.450 --> 00:09:43.730
What is that?

00:09:49.030 --> 00:09:50.730
Please step inside this.

00:10:33.550 --> 00:10:35.430
Wow...

00:10:35.430 --> 00:10:36.940
So this is...

00:10:46.490 --> 00:10:48.870
You who have come seeking information...

00:10:50.870 --> 00:10:52.900
Welcome to Kado.

00:10:56.260 --> 00:11:00.030
There's something we want 
you, as journalists, to see.

00:11:01.930 --> 00:11:07.160
Inside this is another anisotropic 
device, separate from the Wam.

00:11:08.100 --> 00:11:13.190
This one has an effect on the minds of humans.

00:11:14.490 --> 00:11:16.020
Is it dangerous?

00:11:16.020 --> 00:11:20.180
According to Yaha-kui zaShunina, 
it's not especially dangerous.

00:11:20.180 --> 00:11:23.780
However, that has not been 
scientifically investigated,

00:11:23.780 --> 00:11:28.790
so the question comes down to 
whether you trust him or not.

00:11:31.150 --> 00:11:32.400
Let's take a look.

00:11:32.400 --> 00:11:33.080
Gonno-san!

00:11:33.080 --> 00:11:35.940
Can we come this far and run away?

00:11:35.940 --> 00:11:37.670
Well, true, but...

00:11:37.670 --> 00:11:39.140
Oh, jeez...

00:11:39.140 --> 00:11:40.550
We can record, right?

00:11:47.560 --> 00:11:51.070
You humans have already experienced the Wam.

00:11:52.150 --> 00:11:56.490
The purpose of the Wam was to draw 
anisotropic information into the universe,

00:11:56.940 --> 00:11:58.910
but this has another purpose.

00:12:30.390 --> 00:12:32.060
Hey, is this...

00:13:37.820 --> 00:13:38.750
What was that?

00:13:38.750 --> 00:13:39.960
The Sansa.

00:13:40.410 --> 00:13:41.590
Sansa?

00:13:42.360 --> 00:13:47.090
The Sansa is a shape that enables humanity 
to comprehend the anisotropic.

00:13:47.380 --> 00:13:50.680
With just one look at it, 
we can peer into the anisotropic,

00:13:50.680 --> 00:13:54.060
as well as gain a sense for it.

00:13:54.060 --> 00:13:56.840
So what we felt was the 
sensation of the anisotropic?

00:13:57.260 --> 00:14:00.100
It was like there were many of me...

00:14:00.100 --> 00:14:03.610
It felt like something shifted... 
like there were more of me.

00:14:03.610 --> 00:14:07.250
But all of those "me"s were me...

00:14:09.230 --> 00:14:10.950
You are fragments.

00:14:11.630 --> 00:14:14.450
You exist in the universe,

00:14:14.450 --> 00:14:17.710
but that is only a portion of you.

00:14:17.710 --> 00:14:21.740
The majority of you extends 
into higher dimensions.

00:14:22.510 --> 00:14:25.220
In this universe, you simply can't feel it.

00:14:28.900 --> 00:14:32.070
What you think is all of you

00:14:32.930 --> 00:14:35.640
is only a single cross-section
of a greater individual

00:14:36.940 --> 00:14:38.960
that exists across multiple dimensions.

00:14:41.130 --> 00:14:44.280
To be honest, I still can't quite accept that...

00:14:45.020 --> 00:14:48.680
But what does this sensation mean?

00:14:49.500 --> 00:14:51.410
He understands already.

00:14:52.290 --> 00:14:53.190
Like this?

00:14:55.090 --> 00:14:56.010
Like this?

00:14:57.250 --> 00:14:58.250
Like this! Like this!

00:14:58.710 --> 00:15:00.440
It's like this, Emi!

00:15:00.440 --> 00:15:02.630
My eyes are open now.

00:15:02.630 --> 00:15:05.030
But the "me"s in front and behind 
me are closing their eyes.

00:15:05.030 --> 00:15:05.880
You get it, right?!

00:15:05.880 --> 00:15:08.760
I'm opening my eyes and closing 
them at the same time!

00:15:09.120 --> 00:15:11.250
Once you have the sense of the anisotropic,

00:15:11.250 --> 00:15:15.010
one of you can sleep while one remains awake.

00:15:15.620 --> 00:15:18.190
You can work-share yourself.

00:15:18.190 --> 00:15:22.290
It is the Sansa that gives us this new sense.

00:15:23.370 --> 00:15:25.900
A device that makes sleep unnecessary...

00:15:25.900 --> 00:15:29.280
In truth, I haven't slept for twenty days.

00:15:30.610 --> 00:15:34.280
I want to offer this, as well 
as the Wam, to humanity.

00:15:34.280 --> 00:15:38.080
For that, I had you look at it first.

00:15:38.080 --> 00:15:41.800
The form of the Sansa is more 
complex than that of the Wam.

00:15:41.800 --> 00:15:44.640
It's not something that humanity 
can quickly learn to replicate.

00:15:45.300 --> 00:15:47.550
At present, there is only this one,

00:15:47.550 --> 00:15:50.230
and it will take time to produce more.

00:15:50.840 --> 00:15:56.650
But, as you just saw, simply seeing the 
Sansa is enough to produce the effect.

00:15:57.310 --> 00:16:00.320
I turned to the government for 
help in spreading the Wam,

00:16:01.020 --> 00:16:06.510
but I want to turn to you, the media, 
for help in spreading the Sansa.

00:16:10.450 --> 00:16:12.450
They were good humans.

00:16:12.450 --> 00:16:14.340
The ones we just met?

00:16:14.760 --> 00:16:17.720
They have a high degree of 
specialization and a strong vector.

00:16:18.230 --> 00:16:21.620
They have a separate power 
from Shinawa Kanata.

00:16:21.620 --> 00:16:25.540
I like humans like them.

00:16:25.540 --> 00:16:28.090
You have likes and dislikes?

00:16:28.510 --> 00:16:30.880
It's a concept I gained very recently.

00:16:30.880 --> 00:16:32.770
Come to think of it,

00:16:32.770 --> 00:16:35.410
you've been reading a lot of books lately.

00:16:35.850 --> 00:16:39.820
Maybe that's why you're 
seeming a little more human.

00:16:41.890 --> 00:16:43.600
Speaking of books,

00:16:43.600 --> 00:16:45.400
use this if you like.

00:17:12.420 --> 00:17:14.070
What happened?

00:17:14.070 --> 00:17:16.350
Some journalists went inside Kado...

00:17:16.350 --> 00:17:19.140
Yeah, I'll explain.

00:17:19.140 --> 00:17:21.740
This was an irregular event 
that disrupted the plan,

00:17:22.200 --> 00:17:23.900
but a new anisotropic—

00:17:26.520 --> 00:17:28.520
Shindo, what's that sound?

00:17:33.610 --> 00:17:35.690
The sound of a festival, maybe?

00:17:35.690 --> 00:17:38.280
It's been a month since you came here.

00:17:38.640 --> 00:17:40.440
I guess it's that time of year...

00:17:58.070 --> 00:17:59.170
What is this?

00:17:59.640 --> 00:18:01.560
It's called a mask. It's part
of the local culture.

00:18:01.560 --> 00:18:03.830
The rule is that you wear it at a festival.

00:18:03.830 --> 00:18:05.240
Culture?

00:18:05.240 --> 00:18:06.600
I understand.

00:18:06.600 --> 00:18:08.140
Sheesh...

00:18:08.140 --> 00:18:11.120
The chaos it would cause if he 
just walked around like normal...

00:18:12.230 --> 00:18:15.160
You're quite famous yourself, Shindo-kun.

00:18:15.160 --> 00:18:19.990
Seriously, why did I have to change into this?

00:18:19.990 --> 00:18:21.650
Well, zaShunina's learning cultural—

00:18:21.650 --> 00:18:24.450
Why couldn't Natsume-san wear it, then?!

00:18:24.450 --> 00:18:27.070
She's taller than I am!

00:18:27.070 --> 00:18:29.430
She'd look a lot better in a yukata!

00:18:29.430 --> 00:18:33.710
I'm a negotiator! Why must I wear something 
like this that doesn't suit me at all?

00:18:34.260 --> 00:18:36.920
And this goldfish bag, too...

00:18:37.730 --> 00:18:40.270
Shindo-san, tell them!

00:18:40.270 --> 00:18:41.510
No, you look great.

00:18:46.290 --> 00:18:48.340
<b>Treasure Fishing</b>

00:19:39.690 --> 00:19:41.370
What is "buttered potato"?

00:19:41.370 --> 00:19:42.330
Hey!

00:19:43.450 --> 00:19:45.610
Hanamori, we'll split up.

00:19:45.610 --> 00:19:48.160
We can put an emphasis on 
functionality and go by age.

00:19:48.160 --> 00:19:49.700
Understood.

00:19:50.260 --> 00:19:52.250
Natsume, Asano, and I will be group A.

00:19:52.250 --> 00:19:55.780
Sayaka-san, zaShunina, you, 
and the turtle will be in group B.

00:19:56.500 --> 00:19:58.140
That's not fair!

00:19:56.500 --> 00:20:04.330
<b>Okonomiyaki</b>

00:19:58.140 --> 00:20:00.030
I wanna drink, too!

00:20:00.030 --> 00:20:01.760
Someone come here!

00:20:01.760 --> 00:20:03.470
Hanamori-san!

00:20:04.460 --> 00:20:06.540
I'm coming!

00:20:06.950 --> 00:20:08.790
I can finally relax.

00:20:08.790 --> 00:20:12.050
The anisotropic being is 
a lot more easygoing now.

00:20:12.050 --> 00:20:15.270
He's changed a lot over the last month.

00:20:15.270 --> 00:20:17.060
So, Shindo-kun,

00:20:17.900 --> 00:20:19.660
what happened inside?

00:20:22.360 --> 00:20:23.860
Sansa...

00:20:23.860 --> 00:20:26.110
People won't have to sleep?

00:20:26.870 --> 00:20:28.370
What do you think?

00:20:28.370 --> 00:20:31.850
Humans spend about a third 
of their day asleep.

00:20:32.500 --> 00:20:37.350
Without it, human productivity 
would increase by 1.5 times.

00:20:38.130 --> 00:20:41.500
That's going to mean some 
serious efficiency gains.

00:20:43.650 --> 00:20:45.180
Are there any negative affects?

00:20:45.180 --> 00:20:48.350
Like a shortened lifespan?

00:20:48.700 --> 00:20:50.310
We would have to investigate,

00:20:50.310 --> 00:20:52.890
but after having actually experienced it,

00:20:52.890 --> 00:20:54.310
I think it's fine.

00:20:55.150 --> 00:20:56.870
I can still sleep if I want to.

00:20:57.300 --> 00:21:00.280
I just don't have to if I don't want to.

00:21:00.280 --> 00:21:04.490
If there are no downsides, 
it's a really great gift.

00:21:04.490 --> 00:21:06.280
That's the idea.

00:21:07.930 --> 00:21:09.860
I can't really say why yet,

00:21:10.830 --> 00:21:13.910
but how will this development 
lead to happiness?

00:21:14.810 --> 00:21:16.200
That's right.

00:21:16.200 --> 00:21:20.800
Will rapid advancement really 
bring happiness to people?

00:21:21.690 --> 00:21:22.810
No, what I meant was...

00:21:22.810 --> 00:21:26.170
Shindo-san, please come with me, now!

00:21:30.430 --> 00:21:32.030
Lost?

00:21:32.030 --> 00:21:33.770
That guy...

00:21:34.600 --> 00:21:35.690
Shindo-san...

00:21:38.190 --> 00:21:42.190
Yaha-kui zaShunina is with Hanamori-san.

00:21:43.790 --> 00:21:45.900
I lied about him being lost.

00:21:46.580 --> 00:21:47.740
Why?

00:21:48.870 --> 00:21:51.740
I wanted to talk with you alone.

00:21:53.400 --> 00:21:54.900
I have a request.

00:21:54.900 --> 00:21:57.240
I want your help.

00:21:57.750 --> 00:21:59.170
My help?

00:22:00.460 --> 00:22:03.700
I want to send Yaha-kui zaShunina 
back to the anisotropic.

00:23:35.970 --> 00:23:37.010
Go home?

00:23:37.010 --> 00:23:40.600
We can handle things without you for a day.

00:23:40.600 --> 00:23:43.170
Dad! No, it's not like that!

00:23:43.170 --> 00:23:44.770
Shindo-san, say something!

00:23:45.180 --> 00:23:48.070
We are the humans who 
chose to share information.

00:23:48.070 --> 00:23:50.110
We can't run from that.

00:23:48.500 --> 00:23:52.000
Talnel
